                    <td>{int(genre_stats.iloc[1]['Reviews']):,}</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Non-Fiction dominates the bestseller list in volume and commands a slightly higher average price, but Fiction books accumulate significantly more reviews on average, indicating a highly engaged readership.</p>
        <div class="chart-container">
            <img src="{genre_img}" alt="Genre Comparison Charts">
        </div>

        <h2>4. Year-over-Year Trends in Pricing and Ratings</h2>
        <p>Over the decade, there has been a notable downward trend in average bestseller prices, dipping significantly after 2014. Conversely, average user ratings have steadily climbed, suggesting that readers are getting better perceived value (higher satisfaction at lower price points) over time.</p>
        <div class="chart-container">
            <img src="{trends_img}" alt="Trend Line Chart">
        </div>

        <h2>5. Dominant Authors on the Bestseller List</h2>
        <p>Certain authors have established a persistent presence on the top 50 list. Here are the top authors by appearance frequency, along with their pricing and rating metrics:</p>
        <table>
