for _, row in top_authors.iterrows():
    html += f"""
                <tr>
                    <td>{row['Author']}</td>
                    <td>{row['Frequency']}</td>
                    <td>${row['Price']:.2f}</td>
                    <td>{row['User Rating']:.2f}</td>
                </tr>
"""

html += """
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>6. Strategic Recommendations</h2>
        <ul class="recommendations">
            <li><strong>Pricing Strategy:</strong> A high price does not guarantee a high rating (Pearson correlation: """ + f"{correlation:.3f}" + """). Avoid artificially inflating prices under the assumption that it signals premium quality. Instead, price competitively, particularly in Fiction, where lower prices align with higher review volumes.</li>
            <li><strong>Genre Focus:</strong> If the goal is consistent, premium pricing, Non-Fiction offers a higher average price ceiling. However, if the goal is rapid audience engagement and review velocity, Fiction is the superior vehicle.</li>
            <li><strong>Temporal Adaptation:</strong> The steady decline in average bestseller prices over the decade highlights increased price sensitivity and competition. Publishers must optimize production and marketing costs to maintain profitability at the $10-$14 price point, which is becoming the new norm for bestsellers.</li>
            <li><strong>Author Cultivation:</strong> Top authors like Jeff Kinney and Rick Riordan demonstrate that consistent output of highly-rated, moderately-priced books drives repeated bestseller appearances. Invest in long-term author franchises rather than relying solely on one-off high-priced hits.</li>
